cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it."
type: dataset
title: "UK Flood Warnings, captured hourly (wss-flood-warnings)"
abstract: >-
  Hourly point-in-time captures of every live flood alert and warning issued by
  the Environment Agency for England. The publisher documents that a warning is
  set to severity 4, "Warning no longer in force", approximately 24 hours after
  it is raised, and that the record is then removed altogether; the agency's own
  archive contains daily measurement readings only and no warnings at all. The
  Internet Archive holds 57 captures of the warnings endpoint across 2017-2026,
  against a 24-hour turnover, so the great majority of flood events since 2017
  are not recoverable from anywhere. Each capture records severity, the flood
  area, county, river or sea, the EA operational area and region, tidal status,
  and the times the warning was raised and last changed.
authors:
